              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Keeping your trailer on the road starts long before an inspector pulls you over. Understanding DOT trailer inspection requirements helps protect your drivers, avoid costly violations, and reduce unexpected downtime. Whether you manage an entire fleet or operate a single trailer, regular inspections and preventive maintenance are essential for staying compliant and keeping your equipment performing at its best.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we know that trailer uptime is critical to your business. That's why our experienced service team helps customers stay ahead of repairs with professional inspections, quality parts, and dependable service. Our goal is simple: help you spend more time hauling and less time sitting in the shop.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/the-basics-of-dot-trailer-inspection-requirements/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1000,
                      "height": 667,
                      "alt": "Sun State technician logging a trailer inspection on a clipboard in the yard"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-what-are",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Are DOT Trailer Inspection Requirements?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "what-are"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-are-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "DOT trailer inspection requirements are federal safety standards established by the Federal Motor Carrier Safety Administration (FMCSA). These regulations are designed to ensure commercial trailers operate safely on public roads while reducing the risk of accidents caused by equipment failure.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-are-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "In addition to required annual inspections, drivers are expected to perform pre-trip and post-trip inspections to identify potential problems before they become safety hazards.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-are-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>A proper inspection helps verify that critical systems are functioning correctly, including:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-what-are-4",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Brakes"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Tires and wheels"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Suspension"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lights and reflectors"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Coupling devices"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Frame and structural components"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Landing gear"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Safety equipment"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-are-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "According to the FMCSA, regular inspections and preventive maintenance play an important role in reducing roadside violations and improving highway safety.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-checklist",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A Semi Trailer Inspection Checklist Every Fleet Should Follow",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "checklist"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While every operation has unique needs, a thorough semi trailer inspection checklist should cover the major safety components required under DOT trailer regulations.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-checklist-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Braking System",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The braking system is one of the most heavily inspected areas during any DOT inspection. Check for:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-checklist-4",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Air leaks"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Worn brake linings"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Damaged brake chambers"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Slack adjuster operation"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Proper air pressure"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-5",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Brake issues are one of the leading causes of out-of-service violations, making routine inspections especially important.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-checklist-6",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Tires and Wheels",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-7",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Damaged tires don't just create expensive roadside repairs — they also increase the risk of blowouts and accidents. Inspect for:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-checklist-8",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 4
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 20
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "cards-checklist-8-1",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 6
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 22,
                          "paddingRight": 22,
                          "paddingBottom": 22,
                          "paddingLeft": 22
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "cards-checklist-8-1-list",
                          "type": "prose-list",
                          "props": {
                            "ordered": false,
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "text": "Proper tire pressure"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Uneven tread wear"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "cards-checklist-8-2",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 6
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 22,
                          "paddingRight": 22,
                          "paddingBottom": 22,
                          "paddingLeft": 22
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "cards-checklist-8-2-list",
                          "type": "prose-list",
                          "props": {
                            "ordered": false,
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "text": "Sidewall damage"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Loose or cracked wheel components"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Missing lug nuts"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-9",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Catching tire issues early often prevents much larger repair bills later.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-checklist-10",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Lighting and Electrical Components",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-11",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "DOT regulations require all lighting systems to operate properly. Verify that your trailer's brake lights, turn signals, clearance lights, marker lights, and reflectors are all clean, functional, and visible before every trip.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-checklist-12",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Suspension and Frame",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-13",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Your suspension absorbs thousands of pounds of force every day. Inspect for:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-checklist-14",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Broken leaf springs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Worn bushings"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Cracked welds"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Bent frame members"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Loose suspension hardware"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-15",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Ignoring structural damage can quickly lead to more extensive <a href=\"/service\">trailer repair</a> needs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/the-basics-of-dot-trailer-inspection-requirements/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1000,
                      "height": 667,
                      "alt": "Sun State technician checking trailer wheels and coupling in the yard"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-schedule",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Schedule Service With Sun State Trailers",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "schedule"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-schedule-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Don't wait until a failed inspection sidelines your equipment. Our experienced technicians provide comprehensive trailer service, inspections, maintenance, and trailer repair to help keep your fleet compliant and on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-schedule-2-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-schedule-2",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
