                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "co-schedule-2-cta",
                          "type": "buttons",
                          "props": {
                            "align": "left",
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "ctaId": "contact-us",
                                "label": "Contact Us at Sun State →",
                                "style": "link"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-preventive",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventive Maintenance Makes DOT Compliance Easier",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "preventive"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Passing an annual inspection shouldn't be your only goal. The most successful fleets build preventive maintenance into their regular operations instead of waiting for inspection time.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Regular trailer service helps identify worn components before they fail, reducing emergency breakdowns and keeping your equipment compliant throughout the year. Working with a trusted service provider also helps maintain detailed maintenance records, making inspections smoother and providing documentation if questions arise.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mistakes",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common DOT Inspection Mistakes",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mistakes"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistakes-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Many roadside violations are preventable. Some of the most common issues inspectors find include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-mistakes-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Inoperative lights"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Tire tread below legal limits"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Brake adjustment problems"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Missing reflective tape"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Damaged air lines"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Loose coupling components"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Cracked mud flaps"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Incomplete maintenance records"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistakes-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "These small problems may seem minor, but they can result in citations, out-of-service orders, delivery delays, and lost revenue. Routine inspections by qualified technicians significantly reduce these risks.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-year-round",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Stay Inspection Ready Year-Round",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "year-round"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-year-round-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Understanding DOT trailer inspection requirements is about more than checking a compliance box. It's about protecting your drivers, reducing downtime, extending the life of your equipment, and keeping your business moving. Routine inspections, preventive maintenance, and timely repairs all work together to improve reliability and reduce costly surprises on the road. If it's time for your next inspection or your fleet needs dependable trailer service, the team at <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a> is ready to help.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-year-round-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Schedule service with Sun State Trailers today and let our experienced technicians help keep your trailers safe, compliant, and ready for every mile.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "links-year-round-3-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
